  <h1>PRIMORDIA</h1>
  <h2>CHAPTER 2 — INTO THE UNKNOWN</h2>

  <h3>SCENE 1 — ALONE</h3>

  <p class="stage">[The night is silent.]</p>

  <p class="stage">
    Deep inside the forest, Aurel runs without knowing where he is going.
  </p>

  <p class="stage">
    His breathing is heavy. His clothes are torn. His face is covered with dirt and tears.
  </p>

  <p class="stage">
    Behind him, the burning settlement slowly disappears between the trees.
  </p>

  <p class="stage">He doesn't stop.</p>
  <p class="stage">He keeps running.</p>
  <p class="stage">Until his legs finally give way.</p>

  <p class="dialogue"><strong>SFX:</strong> “THUD!”</p>

  <p class="stage">
    [Aurel falls to his knees beneath a massive ancient tree.]
  </p>

  <p class="stage">[For several moments, he doesn't move.]</p>

  <p class="stage">
    [He stares at the ground, trying to catch his breath.]
  </p>

  <p class="dialogue">
    <strong>AUREL:</strong> “Father...”
  </p>

  <p class="stage">[Nothing answers him.]</p>

  <p class="stage">
    [Aurel slowly turns his head toward the direction of the settlement.]
  </p>

  <p class="stage">
    [The glow of the fire can barely be seen through the trees.]
  </p>

  <p class="dialogue">
    <strong>AUREL:</strong> “I should have stayed.”
  </p>

  <p class="stage">[His voice trembles.]</p>

  <p class="dialogue">
    <strong>AUREL:</strong> “I should have stayed with you.”
  </p>
